 "result": "This repo is a Flask-like framework (`tessel`), with different names than Flask.\n\n- **Decorator:** `needs_app_scope`, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps a command callback so it runs inside the app context, which is the Tessel equivalent of Flask's `with_appcontext`.\n- **Shortcut:** use `app.cli.command()` (`AppGroup.command`, `src/tessel/cli.py:413`). It applies `needs_app_scope` automatically, and you can opt out with `needs_app_scope=False`. `app.cli` is an `AppGroup` created at `src/tessel/app.py:338`. Bundles get one too (`src/tessel/bundles.py:49`).\n- **Class that loads the app:** `TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`), a subclass of `AppGroup`. It is the top-level CLI group behind `main()` at `src/tessel/cli.py:1121`. It finds the app through `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`) using `locate_app`/`locate_main_app`.\n\nIf you use plain `@click.command()` on a standalone group, decorate it with `@needs_app_scope` yourself. `AppGroup` handles that for you.",
